# Stray Vessel — scrub T2 basic striker (Color-saturated warrior, Tashkari jambiya)

[title Stray Vessel]
[image monsters/scrub_warrior_2.png]
[blood #6b3aa0]
[stats hp=18]
[trigger road]

* move Attack
  narration: It cuts down with the jambiya, hand sure on the grip.
  narration: The blade comes up point-first, the skin pulsing faster.

* move Defend
  narration: The pulses across its skin slow, off-rhythm. It turns the blade flat.

* move Recover
  narration: It stands very still. The Color it lost runs back into it from somewhere.

* move Tainted Heavy Slow Telegraphed Attack
  narration: It steps in, the slow pulses across its skin go off-rhythm, and the Color floods out of it as it strikes: a violet that hurts to look at.

* intro
The Tashkari camp at the bottom of the wash is empty. Not abandoned;
the cookfire is still smoking and a goat is still tied. But it's empty, and
the standing figure at the far side of the clearing is not Tashkari. It
is naked, vaguely man-shaped, taller than a man, and the skin ripples
in long slow pulses of a violet that hurts to look at directly,
shading to colors you do not have the eyes for. A jambiya hangs in its
grip, point down, blood not yet dry on the blade. The head turns toward
you as you enter the clearing. It does not raise the blade. It does
not need to. It begins to walk.

* win
+give_gold 12
+add_tag killed_stray_vessel_2
The Color leaves it in pulses that get slower and slower until they
stop. The jambiya falls last. Across the clearing the goat is still
tied; the cookfire is still smoking; the Tashkari are still gone.

* lose
The blade finds its line. Across the clearing the goat is still tied
and the cookfire is still smoking, and you are not a problem the wash
needs to remember anymore.
